  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "COLORED JONES POLYNOMIALS WITHOUT TAILS — We exhibit an inﬁnite family of knots with the property that the ﬁrst coeﬃcient of the n-colored Jones polynomial grows linearly with n.\n\n**COLORED JONES POLYNOMIALS WITHOUT TAILS**\n\n*CHRISTINE RUEY SHAN LEE AND ROLAND VAN DER VEEN*\n\n5 pp, 5 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We exhibit an inﬁnite family of knots with the property that the ﬁrst coeﬃcient of the n-colored Jones polynomial grows linearly with n. This shows that the concept of stability and tail seen in the colored Jones polynomials of alternating knots does not generalize naively.\n\n**Outline.** Page 1; Page 2; Page 3; Page 4; Page 5",
